  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper studies approximate amplitude encoding using shallow variational circuits and shows that amplitude-encoding circuits can be compressed by at least 2× in depth with <0.01% loss in final-state fidelity, and up to about 5× compression with <5% infidelity. Using synthetic datasets and noiseless simulation, Grover search, amplitude estimation, and QFT circuits remain robust when the input-state fidelity exceeds roughly 95%. The RY–CNOT ansatz provided the best fidelity-to-depth compression trade-off.",
